From 7abc91997655a22df45c23bd4cebc41a3a1763fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JohnnyC96 <54557697+JohnnyC96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:00:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: frame counter in the window title

The window title shows guest vsyncs per wall second, "<title> | 27.3 fps",
recomputed once per second: one subtraction and compare per presented host
frame and one SetWindowTitle per second. With a hidden window (scripted runs)
the same rate goes to stdout once per second as "[fps] tick N | 27.3 fps", so
a run without any diagnostics still reports its speed.

- runtime/ps2_fps_counter.h: Ps2FpsCounter::update(nowSeconds, vsyncTick)
  returns true once per second with fps() = vsyncs / elapsed; title(base, fps).
- PS2Runtime::run: updates after EndDrawing, sets the title, logs when hidden.

Test: counter windows (no rate under 1 s, 60 vsyncs in 1.0 s = 60.0, 27 in
1.25 s = 21.6, stalled guest = 0) and the title format.
